<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates soar.</title>
<headline>Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates soar.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) vaulted higher on Thursday at the short end of the curve in line with the trend in the overnight market, traders said.</p>
<p>Due to the continued high demand for pesos to cover reserve positions, many banks had to adjust their swap rates in the PHIBOR market.</p>
<p>The six-month and one-year maturities, however, were steady. Dealers said these were not affected because banks view the high interest rates in the overnight market as temporary.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  NOV 7		 NOV 6</p>
<p>    1 W		12 11/16		11  7/8</p>
<p>    2 W		12  5/16		11  3/4</p>
<p>    1 M		11  3/4		 11  1/2</p>
<p>    2 M		11  9/16		11  7/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  9/16		11  1/2</p>
<p>    6 M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    12M		11  3/4		 11  3/4</p>
<p>    VAL		8-Nov		   7-Nov</p>
<p>- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
